{
  "description": "Server-side RFC 6455 frame decoding with PowerUp's v0 limits (docs/protocol.md, \"Framing\"). From the start of the buffer, while at least two bytes remain: RSV bits must be zero (HK-237), the opcode must be continuation, text, binary, close, ping or pong (HK-239), the mask bit must be set (HK-236); a control frame (close, ping, pong) must be final with a 7-bit length of at most 125, a data frame final and not a continuation (HK-238). A 7-bit length of 126 is followed by a 2-byte big-endian length and 127 by an 8-byte one (HK-241); non-minimal encodings are accepted. Each check is made as soon as its bytes are present, the length against maxPayload before any conversion (HK-240), and before the payload arrives. A frame is decoded only once its 4-byte mask key and whole payload are present, the payload XORed with the key; a trailing partial frame stays in the buffer (HK-242). Any violation refuses the whole buffer: no frame of it is returned and nothing is consumed. The listener decodes with maxPayload 1,048,576.",
  "function": "WebSocketFraming.decodeFrames(from:maxPayload:) — input {buffer, maxPayload} (buffer a bytes descriptor), expected {\"frames\": [{\"opcode\", \"payload\"}], \"remaining\"} (payload and remaining bytes descriptors; remaining is the buffer after the call) or {\"error\": \"protocolViolation\"}",
  "verifiedBy": "DESIGN.md v1.7; RFC 6455 section 5; Tests/PowerUpTests/ProtocolFixtureTests.swift testFrameDecodeTable plays it through WebSocketFraming.decodeFrames(from:maxPayload:). Rust: rust/powerup-core/tests/protocol.rs frame_decode_cases runs protocol::framing::decode_frames.",
  "capturedAgainst": "Swift 5.9.2 Foundation and CryptoKit (Xcode 15.2) on macOS 27.2, PowerUp at 2d20afb",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a small text frame",
      "input": {
        "buffer": {
          "hex": "818f112233446a00473d6147117e33525a2a76004e"
        },
        "maxPayload": 1048576
      },
      "expected": {
        "frames": [
          {
            "opcode": "text",
            "payload": {
              "text": "{\"type\":\"ping\"}"
            }
          }
        ],
        "remaining": {
          "hex": ""
        }
      },
      "reason": "The common case: one masked, final text frame (HK-236)."
    },
    {
